    "text": "Conjecture: A finite group is not simple if it has an irreducible complex\ncharacter of odd degree vanishing on a class of odd length.\n    If true, this implies the solvability of groups of odd order, so a proof independent\nof CFSG is of special interest.                                               V. Pannone",
